    "q-130778": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130778",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrices $A$ and $C$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is an elementary matrix.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-130778-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$A$  and $B$ only",
