    "q-31889": {
      "dom_id": "step-q31889",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $D$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $F$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $E$ is an elementary matrix.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
