    "q-42697": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42697",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
